<body>
  <GameNav />
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Rooms &amp; Exits</a> &gt; Chapter 4 &gt; Level 3</nav>

  <main class="seo-section">
    <h1>Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 4 Level 3 Walkthrough: The Office</h1>

    <p>The Office is room <b>3 of 15</b> in Chapter 4, <i>Pharaoh's Bride</i>, and it changes pace completely. Pharaoh's Tomb was one exhibit hall, Power and Security was one machine split across two rooms — this one is a whole floor: an office with a desk, a printer and a bookshelf, a restroom behind the door with the two-figure sign, and a meeting room with a long conference table, a wall screen and the chapter's three motivational posters. You do not repair anything. You pick a pile of small locks apart, one room at a time.</p>

    <p>The spine is short once you see it. The office gives you three items and the digits <b>7 3 6</b> on the posters. The restroom gives you a <b>valve handle</b> for the red pipe and, once the steam is up, four Greek letters on the mirror — which are the answer to the <b>four-slot laptop</b> back in the office. The meeting room holds a credenza with a <b>three-dial lock</b>, three abstract paintings and a second laptop that is dead until you find its charger. The jigsaw that follows pays out a <b>printed photo</b> reading <b>7205</b>, and 7205 is the four-dial lock that hands you the door key at <b>6:38</b>.</p>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Webelinx Games, the developer of Rooms &amp; Exits: Escape Room Games.</div>

    <div class="verify-note">Rebuilt frame by frame at one frame per second from the <b>full 6:46 run</b> (406 frames, 1080p). Three numbers are printed on this page and each was read more than once: <b>7 3 6</b> on the posters (four reads — the wide close-up plus one crop per poster), <b>7205</b> on the printed photo (three reads), and <b>7205</b> again on the four-dial lock as it is turned (two reads), plus the end card's <b>+50</b> and <b>11:04</b> (consistent across every frame that shows the card). Everything that two passes read differently — the mirror letters, the pie-chart slices, the keypad display, the sticky note on the laptop, the efficiency bar on the end card — is listed under &quot;What this page could not verify&quot; instead of being printed as an answer.</div>

    <LevelSelector chapter={4} current={3} variant="jump" label="Chapter 4 · Pharaoh's Bride" />

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>The Office is room 3 of 15 in Chapter 4. The end code is <b>7205</b>, read off the printed photo the jigsaw spits out; the posters carry <b>7 3 6</b>; the mirror carries four Greek letters that open the four-slot laptop.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>In the office take the <b>Stained paper</b> (0:13) and the <b>USB flash drive</b> (0:19), then read the three posters: <b>7 3 6</b> left to right (0:21).</li>
        <li>Take the <b>Decorative cube</b> (0:52) and go through the restroom door.</li>
        <li>In the bathroom take the <b>Paint thinner</b> (1:15) and the red <b>Valve handle</b> (1:18), then fit the handle to the <b>red pipe</b> (1:22) to steam the mirror.</li>
        <li>Read the <b>four Greek letters</b> wiped in the mirror's condensation (1:28), then set the office laptop's four slots to match — the desktop appears at 2:00.</li>
        <li>In the meeting room take the <b>Cloth</b> and combine it with the paint thinner into a <b>Cloth with thinner</b> (2:33); note the three paintings (the middle one carries an <b>I</b>) and the credenza's three-dial lock.</li>
        <li>The second laptop is dead: find its <b>charger</b> (4:29) and plug it in, then solve the <b>jigsaw</b> (4:40–6:04).</li>
        <li>Collect the <b>Printed photo</b> (6:07) — it reads <b>7205</b> — and set the four-dial lock to <b>7205</b> (6:24–6:38). Take the <b>silver key</b>.</li>
        <li>Use the key on the exit door (6:41). The level ends on the Reward card at 6:44: <b>+50</b> coins and <b>Time 11:04</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="video-wrap">
      <div class="yt-facade" data-yt="agedEZeIoG4" data-title="Rooms &amp; Exits Level 3 The Office Walkthrough Chapter 4"
           role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Play video: Rooms &amp; Exits Level 3 The Office walkthrough">
